.SH NAME
mouser\-ssh \- ssh, with TERM=mouser kept where the host knows it and xterm\-256color where it does not (the same as the `ssh` Mouser puts on its tabs\*(Aq PATH); see docs/ssh.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser ssh\fR [\fISSH_ARGS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
ssh, with TERM=mouser kept where the host knows it and xterm\-256color where it does not (the same as the `ssh` Mouser puts on its tabs\*(Aq PATH); see docs/ssh.md.
.PP
Interactive sessions check the server for Mouser\*(Aqs terminfo in the same connection; everything else (scp, sftp, git, \-N/\-W tunnels, \-O, no local terminal) runs the real ssh unchanged. MOUSER_SSH_TERM=auto|mouser|xterm\-256color (or `SetEnv MOUSER_SSH_TERM=…` for a host in ssh_config) overrides it.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
[\fISSH_ARGS\fR]
ssh\*(Aqs own options, destination and command
